  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education and Protection of children and young people (EPCYP) (Uganda)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Northern Uganda is recovering from two decades of severe conflict which ended after a ceasefire agreement in 2006. The region still faces a number of challenges. The government is working to restore the region&apos;s infrastructure and facilities to an adequate level but in the meantime vulnerable children and young people continue to miss out on basic needs and rights such as going to school. Teenage mothers, orphans, children from single parent families, children who were made to fight in the war, and children with disabilities are not getting the help they need. This project will ensure that children and young people, especially girls, are able to receive education or skills training. It will help communities, families and local authorities to better protect and look out for these children themselves in the future. As a result of the project, children will be better educated; young people will have better employment prospects; they will have a greater voice in their communities and be better protected from exploitation and abuse.</narrative>
  </description>
